<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela Manpa in $120 mln deal with Canada Tolko.</title>
<headline>Venezuela Manpa in $120 mln deal with Canada Tolko.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan pulp and paper manufacturer Manpa has signed a letter of intent with Canada's Tolko Company to build two sawmills in Venezuela, an investment of $120 million, Economia Hoy daily reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The plants would be located in the Guayamure and Imataca areas, in southeast Venezuela, the newspaper quoted Manpa President Alejandro Delfino as saying.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 5052600))</p>
</text>
